This JavaScript function validates whether a given string resembles a US street address line. It first checks if the string is a valid USPS postal code and contains state abbreviations. If these conditions are met, it attempts to remove special characters from the string to simplify the validation process. Then it tries to match two or one of the last words against known state abbreviations at the end of the simplified address; it removes this abbreviation part from the string for further processing. The function checks if any part left in the string (either the part matched against the street address pattern before removing the state abbreviation or the entire simplified string after removal) matches the expected street address format and returns `true`/`false` based on the presence of a valid street address element in the input string, respectively.

